    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -760,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        640
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MediaForge H3 — two_stage\n\n1. Choose H3 UNet, compatible turbo LoRA, CLIP and both VAEs in the loaders.\n2. Open Edit Timeline > Resolution / Latent upscale. Select a compatible local H3 latent model. The SELECT_* filename is a placeholder, not a download.\n3. This example uses 672x384 -> 1344x768, 4 total steps, 1 high-resolution step (3 + 1). Timeline settings override Sample Segments width/height.\n4. Uploading a source in generate mode also creates a named video reference. Source purpose and original-audio controls are in the editor.\n5. SelfLift additionally requires Songssx/ComfyUI-MiniMaxH3-TimelineDirector and standard Euler; select an appropriate model/LoRA/schedule combination. General two_stage supports the connected standard sampler.\n\nH3 AV only, 24 fps. Native low/high latent tails are continued independently. Test a short clip at your target size first; no VRAM, speed or seam-quality guarantee.\n\n## Optional image-model post upscale\n\nThe assembled ProRes intermediate feeds Start Video Batch -> ImageUpscaleWithModel -> End Video Batch. Choose a local image upscaler (e.g. OmniSR X2); native model scale determines output size. End keeps source audio and processes 16 frames per batch. This is a separate post process and can be rerun without regenerating H3. ProRes uses more disk than H.264 and remains a lossy intermediate. Per-frame image upscalers may flicker; inspect motion and scene cuts."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MediaForge Timeline — MiniMax H3 long clip (text only)\n\n1. Pick your H3 models in the loaders: fl2va UNet (+ optional turbo LoRA), the Qwen3-VL text encoder (`type = minimax`), the **video** VAE and the **audio** VAE.\n2. Edit the segments in **⏱️ Edit Timeline** (drag the edges; lengths and overlaps stay on the H3 5+17n grid, 24 fps). Each segment has its own prompt.\n3. Queue. 🎛️ Sample Segments generates one segment at a time, carrying the previous tail (video + audio) into the next; 🧵 Assemble Segments writes one MP4.\n\nDefault plan: 3 × 107 frames, overlaps 22 / 39 → **260 frames**, 346,667 samples at 32 kHz. Batch 1 only. Seams are not guaranteed to be invisible. To use reference images / videos / audio, open `timeline_h3_director.json`.\n\n---\n1. 在載入器選好 H3 模型：fl2va UNet（可加 turbo LoRA）、Qwen3-VL text encoder（`type = minimax`）、**video** VAE 與 **audio** VAE。\n2. 在 **⏱️ Edit Timeline** 編輯分段（拖邊界；段長與重疊落在 H3 的 5+17n 格點、24 fps）；每段有自己的 prompt。\n3. 執行。🎛️ Sample Segments 一次生成一段，把上一段尾端（影像 + 音訊）續接進下一段；🧵 Assemble Segments 輸出一個 MP4。\n\n預設計畫：3 × 107 幀、重疊 22 / 39 → **260 幀**、32 kHz 共 346,667 samples。只支援 batch 1；不保證接縫無痕。要用參考圖片／影片／音訊，請開 `timeline_h3_director.json`。"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
